"I came to Kochi in January," I say to Kiran and Sara.
"I got a job at a software company here."
Sara nods.
"I reached the airport in the morning."
"I had two big bags with me."
"I walked to the prepaid taxi counter."
"I booked a taxi."
"The driver came and helped me take the bags."
"I got into the car."
"He asked me for the address."
"I did not know the way."
"I took a piece of paper from my bag."
"The address of my first room was on it."
"I gave that paper to him."
"He read the address."
"Then he smiled and started the car."
"I looked outside through the window."
"Everything was new."
"But I felt very happy."
